      "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
      "revision": 1373470933,
      "text": "Ficus platyphylla is a deciduous tree within the family Moraceae. Common local names include Gamji in Hausa and Gaba or Kobo in Bambara. It is native to western and eastern tropical Africa."
    }
  },
  "sections": {
    "uses": {
      "en": {
        "source": "Wikipedia (en): Ficus platyphylla § Uses",
        "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ficus_platyphylla#Uses",
        "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
        "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
        "retrieved": "2026-10-17",
        "revision": 1373470933,
        "heading": "Uses",
        "text": "The species is used as an antidote to poison in different cultures. In Nigeria, the stem bark extracts of the plant is used in ethnomedicine to treat a variety of ailments including depression, epilepsy and psychosis. It is also used to expel parasitic worms from the body.",
        "truncated": false
      }
    }
